35
00:05:22,779 --> 00:05:25,204
[Vocab] 死没者

36
00:05:25,603 --> 00:05:28,315
[Host] It means the deceased — people who have died.

37
00:05:28,915 --> 00:05:43,603
[Slow] 広島市の松井市長は「平和宣言」を読み上げ、核兵器の廃絶に向けて行動するよう、世界のリーダーに呼びかけました。

38
00:05:44,403 --> 00:05:51,771
[Host] In the peace declaration, the mayor called on world leaders to take action toward abolishing nuclear weapons.

39
00:05:52,372 --> 00:05:54,699
[Vocab] 廃絶

40
00:05:55,100 --> 00:05:58,579
[Host] It means abolition — getting rid of something completely.

41
00:05:59,180 --> 00:06:13,603
[Slow] また、日本政府に対して、核兵器禁止条約の会議にオブザーバーとして参加し、早く条約に入るよう求めました。

42
00:06:14,403 --> 00:06:22,755
[Host] He also urged the Japanese government to attend a meeting on the nuclear weapons ban treaty as an observer, and to join the treaty soon.

43
00:06:23,355 --> 00:06:25,732
[Vocab] 条約

44
00:06:26,132 --> 00:06:30,211
[Host] It means a treaty — a formal agreement between countries.

45
00:06:30,812 --> 00:06:41,108
[Slow] 式典では、子どもの代表の小学生2人が、「平和への誓い」を読み上げました。

46
00:06:41,908 --> 00:06:47,740
[Host] Two elementary school students, representing the children, read out the pledge for peace.

47
00:06:48,339 --> 00:06:50,403
[Vocab] 誓い

48
00:06:50,803 --> 00:06:53,132
[Host] It means a pledge, or vow.

49
00:06:53,732 --> 00:07:07,172
[Slow] 被爆者の平均年齢は86歳を超え、戦争の体験を直接聞くことは、年々難しくなっています。

50
00:07:07,971 --> 00:07:15,555
[Host] The average age of the survivors is now over eighty-six, and hearing their stories directly is getting harder every year.

51
00:07:16,156 --> 00:07:19,060
